import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 646 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 647 | 2026-10-24 | **Rhythm and Posture on the Home follow the Lesson Book (her call); the fold at Clara's ladder joins Notes on the staff.** A new file, lbh.jsx, takes the book's own pages apart (postureLbPages, plLbPages, nvLbPages, tsLbPages, srhLbPages, wsLbPages; nothing copied, so a change in the book shows on the Home): the whole picture is the page's title, words, printed picture and its Remember line under the butler; one by one is the page's 'The words' (its definitions), each 'At the piano' step on its own screen with the printed picture, its tiny tunes one at a time, 'Not like this', and last 'Try it here' with what moved in the online book; your turn keeps the app's questions. Titles now the book's (A steady beat, When the notes stop, Longer notes: 3 and 4 beats, Bars and bar lines, ...). New lessons from book pages the Home had skipped: Posture 'Finger numbers' and 'Finger walks' (Hop on 3 ... Stairs and slide; questions: which finger plays the coral circle, what an empty dashed circle means), Rhythm 'The beat in your fingers' (small-house, big-house and left-hand beats; questions: which finger on the coral beat, tap eight beats). 'Fold at Clara's ladder' (book chapter Line and Space Names, page 5, with its fold animation) sits before Five landmarks in Notes on the staff; questions: where the Queen's G, treble C and Clara land, lines on lines. Posture keeps 'Let the arm carry the hand' as six warm-up screens. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/{patch669.py,lbh.jsx}. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
